      "en": "In this analysis devoted to the triadic community of interpretation (step 5), Royce demonstrates with relentless rigor that philosophical inquiry cannot confine itself to a positivist description of brute facts. The idea is not a mere passive reflection of an external objective reality, but a dynamic intention of the will. For Marcel observing the Roycean dialectic, this priority given to internal purpose reveals the impossibility of dissociating metaphysical truth from the personal commitment of the knowing subject. Royce's Absolute is by no means an immobile substance nor a remote deity of the deists, but an infinite spiritual life that gathers into a concrete and articulated unity the inexhaustible multiplicity of individual experiences without ever dissolving them."
