      "en": "In deepening the mystery of guilt and redemption (development 6), Marcel's analysis of Royce brings to light the decisive turning point leading from the epistemology of truth to a metaphysical ethics of communion. Error itself, far from being pure nothingness, postulates a higher judgment capable of confronting intention with its fulfillment. Thus, Loyalty as defined by Royce intimately prefigures Marcelian 'creative fidelity': it is not a servile obedience to a formal code, but the devoted surrender of oneself to a transpersonal cause that enriches the fabric of human community. At the heart of suffering and betrayal, the atoning act recreates a spiritual order deeper than lost innocence."
