      "en": "Considering the transition from idealism to concrete philosophy (meditation 4), Marcel formulates his masterly appraisal of the Roycean heritage. While Royce relied on the Peircean theory of triadic interpretation to ward off solipsism, Marcel demonstrates that this insight truly culminates in the ontological affirmation of 'We are' (esse est co-esse). The Absolute then ceases to be a speculative concept and becomes the silent Guarantor of our earthly fidelities and promises. By binding the exigence of universality to living incarnation, Royce's thought remains an indispensable milestone for anyone seeking to overcome the impasses of modern nihilism and rediscover the inviolable dignity of the person."
